    {
      "id": "env_override_conditional_loader_side_effects",
      "finding": "At module scope env_override calls CUDA-compatibility and ROCm-symbol helpers before its own import torch. CUDA compatibility defaults off; when enabled and a directory is selected, Python assigns LD_LIBRARY_PATH. This assignment alone establishes no glibc search-path effect. ROCm promotion returns if the separately loaded torch/version.py hip attribute is None; otherwise it may CDLL libtorch_cpu.so with RTLD_GLOBAL, and on failure try an OpenBLAS glob candidate then retry. Exceptions are swallowed. The original Stage A imports torch before vllm, so these helper calls cannot precede its first torch import. The CPU version string alone is not an authenticated value of the hip attribute.",
